Subject: wifi: ath11k: balance bottom halves when returning NSS link descriptors

The NSS link-descriptor notification uses spin_lock_bh() before accessing
the WBM release ring. Both the successful publication and no-entry paths
share an exit which only drops the spinlock, leaving this acquisition's
bottom-half disable nesting in effect. Pair it with spin_unlock_bh().

Keep ring access, descriptor contents and firmware policy unchanged. This
does not qualify callback lifetime, teardown DMA quiescence or throughput.

Upstream-Status: Pending

--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/nss.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/nss.c
@@ -137,5 +137,5 @@ static void ath11k_nss_wifili_link_desc_return(struct ath11k_base *ab,
 
 exit:
 	ath11k_hal_srng_access_end(ab, srng);
-	spin_unlock(&srng->lock);
+	spin_unlock_bh(&srng->lock);
 }
